Is there anything out there on how to write priors for variables that are indicator variables?

Currently the survival model is:

logit(survival[i])<-h1*X[i,4]+h2*X[i,5]

and the priors are

h1~dnorm(0,0.001)
h2~dnorm(0,0.001)

is there a better way to model categorical covariates?

